# .trivyignore — Vulnerabilities that are safe to ignore for this project
#
# This project serves static HTML/CSS/JS files via nginx:1.27-alpine.
# The following CVEs do not impact static file serving workloads and are
# explicitly ignored to reduce CI noise. Each entry includes a justification.
#
# Review this file regularly — remove entries when base images are updated
# or when the threat model changes.

# CVE-2023-44487 - HTTP/2 Rapid Reset DoS; nginx:alpine includes the fix in 1.27+
# CVE-2023-44487

# CVE-2024-6387 - "RegreSSHion" OpenSSH vulnerability; affects sshd,
# not nginx. The container does not run an SSH server. Only relevant if sshd
# is installed and running, which it is not in nginx:alpine.
# CVE-2024-6387

# CVE-2023-4911 - "Looney Tunables" glibc buffer overflow in ld.so; requires
# local attacker access to exploit. Container runs as non-root user and does
# not expose a shell. Not exploitable in this deployment model.
# CVE-2023-4911

# CVE-2024-3094 - XZ Utils backdoor; affects liblzma compiled with malicious
# build. nginx:alpine uses musl libc and does not include XZ Utils. Not present
# in the image.
# CVE-2024-3094

